# =============================================================================
# ApexMail .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# Exclude files not needed in Docker build context to reduce build time and
# image size.
#
# SECURITY (audit 1.9): builds run on the deploy host where the production
# secret store (secrets/, /opt/apexmail/secrets bind) and live datastore
# state (dump.rdb, data/) exist next to the checkout. Everything below MUST
# stay excluded so no image build context ever tar-ships plaintext prod
# secrets or runtime state.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Build outputs (rebuilt in container)
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/target

# Secrets and live local state — NEVER part of a build context
secrets/
dump.rdb
data/
test_output.txt
reports/
.kilo/
.turbo/
.idea/
.venv/
# Belt-and-braces: apps/ai is excluded wholesale below, but the training
# venv is 10s of GB — keep an explicit entry in case apps/ai is ever scoped
# down to a subset directory.
apps/ai/training/.venv

# Development files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv
**/__pycache__/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Documentation: intentionally NOT ignored. The runtime Dockerfiles COPY
# docs/ into the images (services/mail-server/Dockerfile builder stages
# COPY docs; the ai-service serves it as the grounding corpus), so a
# `docs/` exclusion here would break those builds. The previous
# `docs/` + `!docs/` pair cancelled out to exactly this behaviour — it is
# now written down instead of accidental. Do NOT add `docs/` here.
LICENSE

# Test files
**/tests
**/__tests__
**/reports

# Large model artifacts (51GB+ — poison the build context tar)
apps/ai
**/*.safetensors
**/*.gguf
**/*.bin

# Development tools

# Docker files (avoid recursive inclusion)
Dockerfile*
!deploy/**/Dockerfile*
!services/**/Dockerfile*
!apps/**/Dockerfile*
docker-compose*

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
tmp/
